# Line endings and binary safety.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# Commit 79f12a1 rewrote src/TS/tspico_io.py with LF endings. The file had
# been CRLF for its whole history, so every line changed: a 48-line fix read
# as 2425 insertions / 794 deletions, and the file then conflicted with main
# in its entirety because git had no common lines to anchor on. Nothing in
# the repo prevented it or made it visible in review.
#
# The fix is to let git own the decision. The firmware sources below are
# stored LF and checked out CRLF, so an editor that writes LF produces no
# diff at all -- the flip becomes impossible to commit by accident.
#
# SCOPE IS DELIBERATELY NARROW. Most .py in this repo is LF (29 files) and
# only the firmware sources are CRLF (8), so there is no blanket *.py rule --
# that would convert the majority and cause exactly the churn this is meant
# to stop. Same for "SD card/help/*.txt", which is 89 CRLF / 40 LF: worth
# reconciling one day, but not here.

# ─── Firmware sources: CRLF in the working tree, LF in the repo ──────────
# These are the modules frozen into the UF2 (src/TS/), the flash-filesystem
# copies (src/main.py, src/dev_tspico.py) and the archived original.
src/main.py         text eol=crlf
src/dev_tspico.py   text eol=crlf
src/TS/*.py         text eol=crlf
archive/*.py        text eol=crlf

# ─── Binary assets: never convert, never try to diff ─────────────────────
# ROM and tape images are the ground truth this repo reverse-engineers; a
# line-ending conversion would silently corrupt them. Marked explicitly so
# that a future `* text=auto` can't reach them. ROMs/ holds extensionless
# 16K images (TSPICO-11-exrom and friends), hence the directory rule.
ROMs/**             binary
src/rom/**          binary
*.tap               binary
*.rom               binary
*.bin               binary
*.dck               binary
*.uf2               binary
*.mpy               binary
*.png               binary
*.jpg               binary
*.pdf               binary
